 "deepDive": {
  "domain": "Foreign relations",
  "title": "Three relationships, one month of US decisions",
  "body": "**US–Poland: money on the table, decision in Washington.** Poland formally asked for a permanent US base in May, and Defence Minister Kosiniak-Kamysz has named four candidate cities and a cost of about 15 bn zł ([WNP](https://www.wnp.pl/bezpieczenstwo/amerykanska-baza-w-polsce-za-15-mld-zl-wladyslaw-kosiniak-kamysz-ujawnia-szczegoly,1112013.html)). After meeting Hegseth on 10 November he spoke of a Pentagon “green light”, and the two signed a defence-industry declaration of intent; the US side has not confirmed a base, and the decision rests with the White House, expected in early December ([TVN24](https://tvn24.pl/polska/pete-hegseth-spotkal-sie-z-wladyslawem-kosiniakiem-kamyszem-szef-pentagonu-oglosil-kolejny-krok-w-sojuszu-st9332784)). This week the finance minister said the budget will pay, and MON said the Patriot service centre’s site comes within three months. The big unknown is the Pentagon’s Europe posture review, with US media reporting possible cuts of 25,000–40,000 troops in Europe ([OKO.press](https://oko.press/na-zywo/na-zywo-relacja/amerykanskie-miasteczko-w-zachodniej-polsce-moze-powstac-w-2029-roku)).\n\n**US–India: close on trade, rough at the edges.** Goyal says only a few issues remain, and observers now point to the 14–15 December G20 rather than Manila as the target ([Aaj Tak](https://www.aajtak.in/business/news/story/india-us-trade-deal-g20-summit-market-access-piyush-goyal-former-diplomat-nisha-biswal-dpmx-smsr-2695202-2026-11-13)). Russian oil faded as an irritant after an October sanctions waiver, but the Pannun lawsuit against NSA Doval and tighter H-1B rules are live friction points. A Quad leaders’ meeting in Manila around 17 November is still unconfirmed ([ThePrint](https://theprint.in/diplomacy/modi-to-visit-philippines-next-week-to-attend-asean-india-summit-quad-leaders-meet-also-likely/3097204/)).\n\n**Poland–India: quiet follow-through.** Tusk’s October visit set a goal of doubling trade by 2030 and launched defence-industry and counter-terrorism dialogues ([Cavalier](https://www.cavalier.in/cds-ota-current-affairs/2026-10-22/india-poland-tusk-visit-joint-statement-2026)). The classified-information agreement that joint defence work needs is still unsigned, with no public movement this week.\n\n**Analysis:** all three tracks now hinge on US decisions due within about a month: the base and posture review for Poland, the trade deal for India.",
  "links": [
   {
    "label": "TVN24",
